    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.extra\r\n\r\n### Additional info\r\n\r\n```\r\nNVIM v0.12.0-dev-1858+g5f22cf5af3\r\ngit version 2.52.0\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nCurrently, hunks are displayed using the first context line as the item text, even when that line is empty. This can be visually confusing:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/08f82247-9096-4812-b0ba-19ead6050bad\" />\r\n\r\nIn my opinion, it would be better to display the first changed line (that starts with `+` or `-`) instead.",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.extra</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional info</h3>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"NVIM v0.12.0-dev-1858+g5f22cf5af3\ngit version 2.52.0\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">NVIM v0.12.0-dev-1858+g5f22cf5af3\ngit version 2.52.0\n</code></pre></div>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Currently, hunks are displayed using the first context line as the item text, even when that line is empty. This can be visually confusing:</p>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/119845045/529230087-08f82247-9096-4812-b0ba-19ead6050bad.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJnaXRodWIuY29tIiwiYXVkIjoicmF3LmdpdGh1YnVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbSIsImtleSI6ImtleTUiLCJleHAiOjE3OTM1NTI4MDEsIm5iZiI6MTc5MzU1MjUwMSwicGF0aCI6Ii8xMTk4NDUwNDUvNTI5MjMwMDg3LTA4ZjgyMjQ3LTkwOTYtNDgxMi1iMGJhLTE5ZWFkNjA1MGJhZC5wbmc_.fVDCyc4z6q25EmVPbBtnZY1DS1nLMpkdizf_dT1ESbQ\"><img width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/119845045/529230087-08f82247-9096-4812-b0ba-19ead6050bad.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJnaXRodWIuY29tIiwiYXVkIjoicmF3LmdpdGh1YnVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbSIsImtleSI6ImtleTUiLCJleHAiOjE3OTM1NTI4MDEsIm5iZiI6MTc5MzU1MjUwMSwicGF0aCI6Ii8xMTk4NDUwNDUvNTI5MjMwMDg3LTA4ZjgyMjQ3LTkwOTYtNDgxMi1iMGJhLTE5ZWFkNjA1MGJhZC5wbmc_.fVDCyc4z6q25EmVPbBtnZY1DS1nLMpkdizf_dT1ESbQ\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 1080px;; aspect-ratio: 1920 / 1080; background-color: var(--bgColor-muted); border-radius: 6px\" class=\"js-gh-image-fallback\"></a>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In my opinion, it would be better to display the first changed line (that starts with <code class=\"notranslate\">+</code> or <code class=\"notranslate\">-</code>) instead.</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.extra\nAdditional info\nNVIM v0.12.0-dev-1858+g5f22cf5af3\ngit version 2.52.0\n\nDescription\nCurrently, hunks are displayed using the first context line as the item text, even when that line is empty. This can be visually confusing:\n\nIn my opinion, it would be better to display the first changed line (that starts with + or -) instead.",
