    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Currently, hunks are displayed using the first context line as the item text, even when that line is empty.\r\n\r\nThis is not the case. Hunks are displayed using [hunk header](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/6170f606fbdb94bf461635c47962f61dceffe496/lua/mini/extra.lua#L1926) as a text. Git itself is responsible to compute a proper text and it is often not a part of context.\r\n\r\nIt has somewhat smart per-language rules and can also be [configured via Git](https://git-scm.com/docs/gitattributes#_defining_a_custom_hunk_header).\r\n\r\nI think using this directly is the most practical and reasonable choice.",
            "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Currently, hunks are displayed using the first context line as the item text, even when that line is empty.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is not the case. Hunks are displayed using <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/6170f606fbdb94bf461635c47962f61dceffe496/lua/mini/extra.lua#L1926\">hunk header</a> as a text. Git itself is responsible to compute a proper text and it is often not a part of context.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It has somewhat smart per-language rules and can also be <a href=\"https://git-scm.com/docs/gitattributes#_defining_a_custom_hunk_header\" rel=\"nofollow\">configured via Git</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I think using this directly is the most practical and reasonable choice.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Currently, hunks are displayed using the first context line as the item text, even when that line is empty.\n\nThis is not the case. Hunks are displayed using hunk header as a text. Git itself is responsible to compute a proper text and it is often not a part of context.\nIt has somewhat smart per-language rules and can also be configured via Git.\nI think using this directly is the most practical and reasonable choice.",
